# What does NOT belong in the published extension.
#
# node_modules is NOT excluded, deliberately: vscode-languageclient is a
# runtime dependency (src/language-client.js requires it when the language
# server is enabled), so dropping it would break that feature for anyone who
# turns the setting on. vsce warns about the file count; bundling is the real
# answer and is a separate job.

# Test harnesses. They run from a checkout against the repo, never from an
# installed extension.
tools/**

# The maintainer reference. README.md is what the install page shows and what
# a user needs; DEVELOPING.md is for people changing the extension, and lives
# in the repository for them.
DEVELOPING.md

# Build leavings.
**/*.map
**/.DS_Store
.vscodeignore
